Nested exception reporting (report once)
  reports once through two levels of nested call! (depth 3)
  reports once when re-raised through a nested call! (depth 2)
  reports a top-level unhandled exception once (baseline)
  still fires each action's own on_exception callback at its level (only the global report is deduped)
  reports at most once, at the innermost action — no ancestor retry when the attempt raises
  dedup/classification is scoped to one execution, not stored on the exception forever
    reports the same exception object again when re-raised by a later, independent run
    does not inherit report-dedup state leaked from a prior run (entry-guard reset)
    dedupes by object identity even when exceptions are value-equal (==/eql?)
    does not let a stale fails_on classification suppress a later independent run
  a fails_on classification is sticky across nested call!
    treats a fails_on-reclassified exception as a failure (no report, failure outcome) when bubbled via call!
    reports outcome `failure` to an ancestor's on_error, even though it runs before the context flag is set
    does NOT make an unrelated same-class exception a failure (tag is per-object, not per-class)
    stays sticky through two levels of call!
    keeps an already-reported inner exception reported even when an ancestor's fails_on reclassifies it to failure

