    adds a null branch to a union type's anyOf
    does not leak a mutation of the returned enum array back into the contract's inclusion validation (Bug CC)
    does not add null to the enum for a non-nil-allowed inclusion field
  a dotted `on:` PARENT or an `on:` pointing at another subfield nests recursively and forces its ancestor chain required when a descendant is required
    requires the top-level root when only a DEEP leaf (subfield-of-a-subfield) is required
    does not require a defaulted top-level root whose only descendant is an optional dotted-parent subfield when its non-blank default satisfies its own contract
    still requires a defaulted top-level root whose only descendant is an optional dotted-parent subfield when its default is a blank {} (runtime rejects the omitted call: "Address can't be blank")
    requires an allow_nil parent through both a required SHALLOW child and its dotted-deep analog
    requires a nil-tolerant root when its shallow child is required, even alongside a deep chain
  a subfield default resolves only the child (value-level on the read path), never materializing the parent
    still requires the parent when a subfield carries a default and no child is required
    still requires the parent when the subfield has no default at all
    still requires the parent when a subfield carries a false default (the default resolves the child's value, not the parent)

